    {
      "id": "s33vjburtcy4f",
      "title": "Why 45 degrees?",
      "createdAt": 1790131728000,
      "updatedAt": 1790131827694,
      "messages": [
        {
          "role": "user",
          "content": "why is max range at 45 degrees intuitively",
          "ts": 1790131748369
        },
        {
          "role": "assistant",
          "content": "Range = (horizontal speed) × (time in the air).\n\n- Steeper angle → longer flight but slower horizontally.\n- Flatter angle → fast horizontally but lands quickly.\n\nThe product v0 cos α · 2v0 sin α / g = v0² sin 2α / g is maximised when sin 2α = 1, i.e. **α = 45°** — the best compromise. Your graph tag on page 2 shows the curve peaking there.",
          "ts": 1790131827694
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
